      "content": "Layout Structure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The design contains several styled images and texts. But before styling each card, let's only focus on the main structure."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<div class=\"projects-grid\">\n2    <!-- Fill layout with dummy items -->\n3    <div></div>\n4    <div></div>\n5    <div></div>\n6    <div></div>\n7    <div></div>\n8    <div></div>\n9</div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1.projects-grid {\n2    display: grid;\n3\n4    /* Define layout's structure */\n5    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr;\n6\n7    /* Temporary row height */\n8    grid-template-rows: 300px 300px;\n9\n10    /* Space out items */\n11    gap: 20px;\n12}\n13\n14.projects-grid > div {\n15    /* Fill all items for visibility */\n16    background-color: gray;\n17}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Browser Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Layout Structure",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the grid layout has six areas, with a 20px gap between each one."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We've also filled each grid area with dummy <div> elements. For better visibility, we've set the background color of each grid item to gray."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The .projects-grid > div child selector allows us to easily apply styles to all <div> elements inside the .projects-grid container."
    },
